.TH AWT 1 "" "awt 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
awt \- a memory for AI agents that lives in plain files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awt
[global flags] VERB [ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
awt records decisions, questions, links and handoffs for an agent task in plain files, and recalls them in the next session.
It never runs a command it is asked to track. See SPEC.md and docs/concepts.md in the repository.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-dir PATH
use the node at PATH instead of the current directory
.TP
.B \-\-by NAME
who is writing (default $AWT_BY, else agent)
.TP
.B \-\-model ID
model that produced this write (default $AWT_MODEL, else unknown:unset)
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version
.SH VERBS
.SS init
Create a task directory, or a node of the tree with \-\-kind.
.PP
.B awt init [\-\-goal GOAL] [\-\-done DONE] [\-\-kind KIND] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-key KEY] [\-\-child CHILD] [\-\-hooks HOOKS] [\-\-uninstall]
.TP
.B \-\-goal GOAL
what this task is for (250 characters)
.TP
.B \-\-done DONE
what finished looks like (250 characters)
.TP
.B \-\-kind KIND
make a node of this kind under the nearest enclosing node (see SPEC.md, Node tree)
.TP
.B \-\-name NAME
directory name of the new node
.TP
.B \-\-key KEY
stable key of the new node, such as paseo:agent/ID
.TP
.B \-\-child CHILD
make (or find) the child node agents/RUN_KEY for a subagent you launch, and print its AWT_DIR and AWT_BY (lowercase letters, digits, \-; at most 40)
.TP
.B \-\-hooks HOOKS
person only, ask first: install the context hooks (after compaction and /clear, and at the first prompt on claude and pi) for claude, codex, opencode, pi or all (edits that provider's own config)
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
with \-\-hooks: remove the hook again
.SS resume
Print the brief: goal, state, open questions and effects, what changed since the last handoff.
.PP
.B awt resume [\-\-hook] [\-\-framed] [\-\-scope SCOPE] [\-\-json]
.TP
.B \-\-hook
print nothing and exit 0 when there is no task or on any error (for a session\-start hook)
.TP
.B \-\-framed
with \-\-hook: put the one\-line reference\-only frame above the brief (prints nothing unless \-\-dir or AWT_DIR names a node; the hooks from init \-\-hooks set this up)
.TP
.B \-\-scope SCOPE
show the state of this scope only
.TP
.B \-\-json
machine\-readable output
.SS list
List what is known about the task, one section or all.
.PP
.B awt list [\-\-all] [\-\-json] [\-\-since SINCE] [\-\-down] SECTION
.TP
.B SECTION
one section: refs, context, docs, outbox, misc, decisions, questions, effects, notes, state, nodes or tree
.TP
.B \-\-all
include superseded, answered and finished items
.TP
.B \-\-json
machine\-readable output
.TP
.B \-\-since SINCE
only records after this ISO 8601 time
.TP
.B \-\-down
include the nodes below this one
.SS find
Search records and files; \-\-like ranks related records from the whole tree.
.PP
.B awt find [\-\-up] [\-\-down] [\-\-tree] [\-\-like LIKE] [\-\-limit LIMIT] [\-\-sessions] [\-\-hook] TERM
.TP
.B TERM
text to look for (case\-insensitive, literal)
.TP
.B \-\-up
search ancestors
.TP
.B \-\-down
search descendants
.TP
.B \-\-tree
search the whole tree under the nearest root
.TP
.B \-\-like LIKE
rank related decisions, answers and notes from every workspace in the tree for this sentence
.TP
.B \-\-limit LIMIT
most results to print
.TP
.B \-\-sessions
also search ingested session text (needs store.db)
.TP
.B \-\-hook
with \-\-like \-: the first\-prompt recall for a hook (reads the prompt on stdin; prints nothing and exits 0 unless an agent node gets related records)
.SS state
Leave the handoff: where things stand and what comes next.
.PP
.B awt state \-\-now NOW \-\-next NEXT [\-\-scope SCOPE]
.TP
.B \-\-now NOW
where things stand
.TP
.B \-\-next NEXT
what the next session should do
.TP
.B \-\-scope SCOPE
name of a sub\-unit of work
.SS note
Record a small fact for later.
.PP
.B awt note TEXT
.TP
.B TEXT
the fact
.SS decide
Record a choice and its reason.
.PP
.B awt decide \-\-why WHY [\-\-supersedes SUPERSEDES] [\-\-tag TAG] [\-\-related RELATED] CHOICE
.TP
.B CHOICE
the choice
.TP
.B \-\-why WHY
the reason (required)
.TP
.B \-\-supersedes SUPERSEDES
id of the earlier decision this replaces
.TP
.B \-\-tag TAG
tag the decision; `rule` binds every later agent; `profile:light|build\-heavy|media\-device` overrides a project's placement class (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-related RELATED
related records to print after writing (0 turns it off)
.SS ask
Record a question for a person.
.PP
.B awt ask [\-\-related RELATED] TEXT
.TP
.B TEXT
the question
.TP
.B \-\-related RELATED
related records to print after writing (0 turns it off)
.SS answer
Answer a question.
.PP
.B awt answer ID TEXT
.TP
.B ID
question id, such as q\-1a2b3c4d
.TP
.B TEXT
the answer
.SS ref
Record a link instead of copying its content.
.PP
.B awt ref \-\-title TITLE [\-\-why WHY] [\-\-kind KIND] [\-\-no\-access] TARGET
.TP
.B TARGET
URL or path; tool\-call:ID links a child node to the call that launched it
.TP
.B \-\-title TITLE
short title (required)
.TP
.B \-\-why WHY
why it matters
.TP
.B \-\-kind KIND
override the guessed kind; `sync` declares the private git remote of a two\-host tree (target: its URL)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-access
mark a link the agent cannot open, so it asks a person to paste it
.SS capture
Save pasted text that cannot be linked into context/.
.PP
.B awt capture \-\-from FROM \-\-title TITLE [\-\-ref REF] FILE
.TP
.B FILE
file to read; stdin when absent or \-
.TP
.B \-\-from FROM
where it came from, such as slack (required)
.TP
.B \-\-title TITLE
short title (required)
.TP
.B \-\-ref REF
URL of the original
.SS status
Set the task status; done is refused while questions or effects are open.
.PP
.B awt status active|paused|done
.TP
.B VALUE
active, paused or done
.SS doctor
Check the task: layout, git and its remotes, disk, settings, store. Prints ok, warn or fail per check.
.PP
.B awt doctor [\-\-staged]
.TP
.B \-\-staged
scan staged git changes for secrets, and staged ledgers for a torn tail, changed rows and conflict markers (for .git/hooks/pre\-commit)
.SS ingest
Copy agent transcripts into the store and update store.db; with \-\-event, record one tool call.
.PP
.B awt ingest [\-\-source SOURCE] [\-\-hook] [\-\-rebuild] [\-\-stdin] [\-\-event]
.TP
.B \-\-source SOURCE
claude, pi, opencode, paseo, ccusage (usage totals) or all; default claude
.TP
.B \-\-hook
silent, exit 0 on any error (for a hook)
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild
delete store.db and build it again from the stored logs
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
read plugin events from stdin (with \-\-source paseo)
.TP
.B \-\-event
read one tool\-call event on stdin and record a detected effect
.SS ui
Browse store.db in a read\-only web page (needs datasette).
.PP
.B awt ui [\-\-port PORT] [\-\-print\-metadata]
.TP
.B \-\-port PORT
port on 127.0.0.1 (default 8777)
.TP
.B \-\-print\-metadata
print the page metadata and exit
.SS help
Print this summary; help agents prints the agent reference.
.PP
.B awt help
.SS effect
Declare an outbound send so it is made once: plan, begin, mark, show.
.PP
.B awt effect
.SS effect plan
Declare a send before it happens.
.PP
.B awt effect plan \-\-target TARGET [\-\-body BODY] [\-\-how HOW] [\-\-after AFTER] [\-\-again] [\-\-why WHY]
.TP
.B \-\-target TARGET
where it goes, such as slack:#eng (required)
.TP
.B \-\-body BODY
file holding the text to send
.TP
.B \-\-how HOW
the command you will run (text only; awt never runs it)
.TP
.B \-\-after AFTER
id of an effect that must be sent first (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-again
plan a send of something already sent
.TP
.B \-\-why WHY
the reason
.SS effect begin
Claim a planned send; send it yourself after this.
.PP
.B awt effect begin ID
.TP
.B ID
effect id, such as e\-3c91d0aa
.SS effect show
Print one effect: state, attempts, how, body.
.PP
.B awt effect show ID
.TP
.B ID
effect id
.SS effect mark
Record how a send ended.
.PP
.B awt effect mark [\-\-ref REF] [\-\-why WHY] ID TO
.TP
.B ID
effect id
.TP
.B TO
sent, not\-sent (needs \-\-why), unknown (needs \-\-why) or dropped
.TP
.B \-\-ref REF
link to the sent item
.TP
.B \-\-why WHY
the reason
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 1 refused, 2 usage error, 3 permission denied, 4 no task or id.
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/reference/ in the repository, one page per verb; `awt help agents`.
